WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Translating Spanish “ponme un café” literally as “put me a coffee” in London sounds abrupt and confusing.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Predict which parts build a natural request in a British café and how to ask for takeaway.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Combine three blocks: “Could I have”, the drink and size, plus “please”, adding “to take away” in the UK.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Practice: choose between the literal calque, “Could I have a small latte to take away, please?”, or a blunt demand.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Option B pairs polite “Could I have” with British “to take away” and “please”.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Reuse the exact same frame for tap water in a restaurant or a return ticket at a UK station.
